# Telegram Bot Safety

- Telegram webhook and Telegram Business message paths are safety-critical. Audit routing before changing handlers, commands, callbacks, or delivery code.
- Coach-only gates must stay intact for admin commands, callbacks, report approval, athlete linking, and break-glass actions.
- Prefer student lookup by `chat_id`. Username-only matching is weaker and must not auto-bind a student without explicit reasoning and manual safeguards.
- No athlete-facing Telegram message may be sent automatically unless the task explicitly preserves an existing coach approval flow.
- Weekly report send, action approval, and TrainingPeaks-related follow-up remain coach-gated.
- Every callback handler must be checked for coach-only access and wrong-student risk.
- Telegram Business paths need extra review because they can bridge coach actions into student chats.
- Any change to Telegram delivery must include a routing trace and manual QA notes covering who can trigger the path, who receives the message, and why no athlete auto-send was introduced.
